---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
const title='About VoxelCurve';
const description='About VoxelCurve, a local-first Minecraft building geometry workspace for circles, ovals and domes.';
const canonical='https://voxelcurve.com/about';
const schemas=[breadcrumbSchema([{name:'VoxelCurve',url:'https://voxelcurve.com/'},{name:'About',url:canonical}])];
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} {canonical} {schemas}>
  <section class="resource-hero"><div class="container"><div class="resource-hero-grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">About the project</span><h1>Built for precise block construction.</h1><p>VoxelCurve turns Minecraft building geometry into exact, practical construction plans that can be followed while you are in-game.</p></div>
    <div class="resource-meta"><span>LOCAL-FIRST</span><strong>No account · No server geometry</strong><small>Blueprint math runs in your browser.</small></div>
  </div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container editorial-grid">
    <aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="section-kicker">01 / Purpose</div><p>A small, focused builder utility instead of a general Minecraft portal.</p></aside>
    <div class="prose editorial-prose">
      <h2>What VoxelCurve does</h2>
      <p>VoxelCurve focuses on circles, ovals and domes. It converts dimensions into deterministic block geometry, exact row or layer segments, material counts and guided build progress.</p>
      <p>The project deliberately avoids unrelated Minecraft content such as news, skins, seeds, servers and general wiki pages. The goal is to solve one construction problem well.</p>
      <h2>Local-first by design</h2>
      <p>Geometry generation, build instructions, PNG images, printable plans, TXT plans, QR generation and supported Litematic exports are created in your browser. No VoxelCurve account is required.</p>
      <p>Build progress is stored locally on the current device and browser. Shared blueprint links contain shape settings in the URL fragment, but they do not include completion progress.</p>
      <h2>One geometry source</h2>
      <p>The blueprint, material count, guided instructions and exports all derive from the same geometry result. This reduces the chance that one part of the site reports a different shape or block count from another.</p>
      <h2>Open maintenance</h2>
      <p>VoxelCurve is the project maintaining this site and its building guidance. The <a href="https://github.com/chenmu2024/VoxelCurve">public source repository</a> documents the implementation and changes; the <a href="https://github.com/chenmu2024/VoxelCurve/blob/main/GEOMETRY.md">geometry specification</a> explains the grid convention and limits. For support, use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
      <p>Technical issues can be reported through the <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/chenmu2024/VoxelCurve/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer">VoxelCurve GitHub issue tracker</a>. Please avoid posting personal, confidential or security-sensitive information in a public issue.</p>
      <h2>Independent project</h2>
      <p>VoxelCurve is an independent fan-made building utility and is not affiliated with Mojang Studios or Microsoft.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
